{"toolCallId":"call_147919a1a91f4486be93784556ddab91","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables appear below. `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `D` is a one-file fixture folder holding three `[TODO: ...]` markers and four content lines, which the script scores at `Overall Completion: 25%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Build the 25% fixture and record the current behavior (`$D`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$D\"` prints `Overall Completion: 25%` and exits 0.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the option is absent today (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$D\"` prints `ERROR: Unexpected argument: 90` and exits 1.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the existing suite is green (`tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the threshold global beside the other option globals (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'MIN_PERCENT=' \"$S\"` prints the empty default declaration.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent` case to the argument loop with a value validation that exits 1 on a missing, non-integer or out-of-range value (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each print an error and exit 1.\n- [ ] T006 Compare the reported integer against the threshold after the output call and exit 3 when it is lower (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$D\"` still prints the full report and exits 3.\n- [ ] T007 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and record exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints the `--min-percent <N>` line, and `rg -n 'below --min-percent threshold' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Add vitest cases for exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at and above it, and exit 1 for an invalid value (`tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .` exits 0 with the new cases listed.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Capture both reports on one folder and diff them (`$S`). Verify: `diff` of the `--min-percent 50` capture and the plain capture prints nothing, with exit statuses 3 and 0.\n- [ ] T010 Check the boundary where the threshold equals the printed percentage (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 25 \"$D\"` exits 0 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 26 \"$D\"` exits 3.\n- [ ] T011 Check the `--file` path (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --file \"$D/spec.md\" --min-percent 90` prints the single-file report and exits 3.\n- [ ] T012 Run the whole cli test project (`runtime/cli`). Verify: `npm test` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The two captured reports are byte-identical and the gate exits 3 on the 25% fixture\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables appear below. `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `D` is a one-file fixture folder holding three `[TODO: ...]` markers and four content lines, which the script scores at `Overall Completion: 25%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Build the 25% fixture and record the current behavior (`$D`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$D\"` prints `Overall Completion: 25%` and exits 0.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the option is absent today (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$D\"` prints `ERROR: Unexpected argument: 90` and exits 1.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the existing suite is green (`tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the threshold global beside the other option globals (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'MIN_PERCENT=' \"$S\"` prints the empty default declaration.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent` case to the argument loop with a value validation that exits 1 on a missing, non-integer or out-of-range value (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each print an error and exit 1.\n- [ ] T006 Compare the reported integer against the threshold after the output call and exit 3 when it is lower (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$D\"` still prints the full report and exits 3.\n- [ ] T007 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and record exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints the `--min-percent <N>` line, and `rg -n 'below --min-percent threshold' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Add vitest cases for exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at and above it, and exit 1 for an invalid value (`tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`). Verify: `npx vitest run tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .` exits 0 with the new cases listed.\n- [ ] T013 Emit a boolean `min_percent_met` field in the `--json` output when `--min-percent` is also passed, true when the reported percentage is at or above N and false otherwise, covering REQ-007 (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 25 \"$D\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` and `bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$D\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Capture both reports on one folder and diff them (`$S`). Verify: `diff` of the `--min-percent 50` capture and the plain capture prints nothing, with exit statuses 3 and 0.\n- [ ] T010 Check the boundary where the threshold equals the printed percentage (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 25 \"$D\"` exits 0 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 26 \"$D\"` exits 3.\n- [ ] T011 Check the `--file` path (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --file \"$D/spec.md\" --min-percent 90` prints the single-file report and exits 3.\n- [ ] T012 Run the whole cli test project (`runtime/cli`). Verify: `npm test` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The two captured reports are byte-identical and the gate exits 3 on the 25% fixture\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_291dc584348d4ff593d172c29475b4d0","title":"Search for 'T###|task id|renumber|sequential'","kind":"search","locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references"}],"rawInput":{"query":"T###|task id|renumber|sequential","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"grep"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_328b624e49944424bb5cf8a4d06da706","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"The completeness calculator prints a percentage and always exits 0, so a caller cannot gate on it. Add a --min-percent <N> option that turns the printed percentage into an exit status without changing the output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `detached HEAD` (created with `--skip-branch`, so no branch exists) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then always exits 0 on a successful run, so a caller that wants to block on a threshold has to parse the printed number. No option accepts a threshold: `--min-percent 90` falls through the argument loop to the positional branch and the run dies with `ERROR: Unexpected argument: 90`.\n\n### Purpose\nLet a caller gate on the percentage it already prints: `--min-percent <N>` exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise, with output identical in both cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n\nThe fixture below is a one-file folder with three `[TODO: ...]` markers and four content lines. Both runs are against the unmodified script.\n\n```text\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh \"$D\"\nOverall Completion: 25%\nTotal Placeholders: 3\nTotal Content Lines: 4\n$ echo $?\n0\n\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$D\"\nERROR: Unexpected argument: 90\nUse --help for usage information\n$ echo $?\n1\n```\n\nSection 2's Problem Statement quotes both exit codes above: a 25% folder exits 0, and the option itself is rejected with exit 1. The `25%` figure is `(1 - 3 / 4) * 100`, rounded to an integer by the script.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--min-percent <N>` option to `calculate-completeness.sh` that exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise.\n- Validate N as an integer in `0..100`, exiting 1 with a message on stderr before any analysis when it is missing or invalid.\n- Compare the percentage the run already reports: `Overall Completion` in folder mode, the single file's `Completion` under `--file`.\n- Add the option to `--help` and record exit 3 in the script's trailing exit-code comment block.\n- Cover the new exit statuses in the existing vitest file.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Any change to the printed report - the requirement is byte-identical stdout, so no line, label or percentage is added or reordered.\n- Any change to how the percentage is computed - rounding, clamping and placeholder patterns stay as they are.\n- Changing exit codes for the existing failure paths - a missing folder, a missing `bc` and an unexpected argument keep exiting 1.\n- Documentation outside the packet - `runtime/cli/README.md` and the skill README are not touched by this change.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, validate it, compare the reported percentage, exit 3 below the threshold, add the help line and the exit-code comment |\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts | Modify | Add cases for exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at or above it, and exit 1 for an invalid value |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` without changing the report. | On one folder, the run with `--min-percent 50` and the run without it produce byte-identical stdout: `diff` of the two captures prints nothing. |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported percentage is below N. | On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 90` prints the unchanged report and exits 3. |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported percentage is at or above N. | On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 25` and `--min-percent 0` each print the unchanged report and exit 0. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range value with exit 1 and a message on stderr, before any analysis. | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each print an error and exit 1, and none of them prints a report. |\n| REQ-005 | Compare the percentage the run reports, in both modes. | In folder mode the comparison uses `Overall Completion`; with `--file <path> --min-percent 90` a file whose `Completion` is below 90 exits 3 and prints the unchanged single-file report. |\n| REQ-006 | Document the option where the script already documents its options. | `--help` prints a line for `--min-percent <N>`, and the trailing exit-code comment block names exit 3 as \"below --min-percent threshold\". |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 and the same run without the option exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: Stdout is byte-identical with and without the option on the same folder, so `diff` of the two captures prints nothing.\n- **SC-003**: A threshold equal to the printed percentage never fails the run: `--min-percent 25` on the 25% fixture exits 0.\n- **SC-004**: The existing vitest suite for the script exits 0 with the new cases included.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` and `bc`, both already required by the script | None new - the script already exits 1 when `bc` is absent | Reuse the existing `bc` presence check and integer comparison; add no new tool |\n| Risk | Exit 3 is also the general `spec/*.sh` system-error code | A caller cannot tell \"below threshold\" from \"system error\" by code alone across the script family | Inside this script the system-error paths exit 1 today, so 3 is unambiguous here; record the meaning in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code block |\n| Risk | The comparison drifts from the printed value, e.g. comparing an unrounded `bc` result | The gate and the report disagree | Compare the same rounded integer variable the report prints, and test the boundary where N equals the printed percentage |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns a non-zero comparison into a silent early exit before the report prints | The report disappears on a failing threshold | Make the comparison the last step before the existing `exit`, and assert in a test that the report still prints when the run exits 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. Decisions taken: the option compares the percentage the run reports (`Overall Completion` in folder mode, `Completion` under `--file`); `--json` output is unchanged because only the exit status differs; an invalid value exits 1 rather than 3 so a caller can separate a bad invocation from a failed gate.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"The completeness calculator prints a percentage and always exits 0, so a caller cannot gate on it. Add a --min-percent <N> option that turns the printed percentage into an exit status without changing the output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `detached HEAD` (created with `--skip-branch`, so no branch exists) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an `Overall Completion` percentage and then always exits 0 on a successful run, so a caller that wants to block on a threshold has to parse the printed number. No option accepts a threshold: `--min-percent 90` falls through the argument loop to the positional branch and the run dies with `ERROR: Unexpected argument: 90`.\n\n### Purpose\nLet a caller gate on the percentage it already prints: `--min-percent <N>` exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise, with output identical in both cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n\nThe fixture below is a one-file folder with three `[TODO: ...]` markers and four content lines. Both runs are against the unmodified script.\n\n```text\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh \"$D\"\nOverall Completion: 25%\nTotal Placeholders: 3\nTotal Content Lines: 4\n$ echo $?\n0\n\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 \"$D\"\nERROR: Unexpected argument: 90\nUse --help for usage information\n$ echo $?\n1\n```\n\nSection 2's Problem Statement quotes both exit codes above: a 25% folder exits 0, and the option itself is rejected with exit 1. The `25%` figure is `(1 - 3 / 4) * 100`, rounded to an integer by the script.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--min-percent <N>` option to `calculate-completeness.sh` that exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise.\n- Validate N as an integer in `0..100`, exiting 1 with a message on stderr before any analysis when it is missing or invalid.\n- Compare the percentage the run already reports: `Overall Completion` in folder mode, the single file's `Completion` under `--file`.\n- Add the option to `--help` and record exit 3 in the script's trailing exit-code comment block.\n- Cover the new exit statuses in the existing vitest file.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Any change to the printed report - the requirement is byte-identical stdout, so no line, label or percentage is added or reordered.\n- Any change to how the percentage is computed - rounding, clamping and placeholder patterns stay as they are.\n- Changing exit codes for the existing failure paths - a missing folder, a missing `bc` and an unexpected argument keep exiting 1.\n- Documentation outside the packet - `runtime/cli/README.md` and the skill README are not touched by this change.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, validate it, compare the reported percentage, exit 3 below the threshold, add the help line and the exit-code comment |\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts | Modify | Add cases for exit 3 below the threshold, exit 0 at or above it, and exit 1 for an invalid value |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` without changing the report. | On one folder, the run with `--min-percent 50` and the run without it produce byte-identical stdout: `diff` of the two captures prints nothing. |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported percentage is below N. | On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 90` prints the unchanged report and exits 3. |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported percentage is at or above N. | On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 25` and `--min-percent 0` each print the unchanged report and exit 0. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range value with exit 1 and a message on stderr, before any analysis. | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1` and `--min-percent 101` each print an error and exit 1, and none of them prints a report. |\n| REQ-005 | Compare the percentage the run reports, in both modes. | In folder mode the comparison uses `Overall Completion`; with `--file <path> --min-percent 90` a file whose `Completion` is below 90 exits 3 and prints the unchanged single-file report. |\n| REQ-006 | Document the option where the script already documents its options. | `--help` prints a line for `--min-percent <N>`, and the trailing exit-code comment block names exit 3 as \"below --min-percent threshold\". |\n| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent <N>` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean `min_percent_met` field: true when Overall Completion is at or above N, false otherwise. | On the 25% fixture, `--json --min-percent 25` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` and `--json --min-percent 90` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false`. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: On the 25% fixture, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 and the same run without the option exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: Stdout is byte-identical with and without the option on the same folder, so `diff` of the two captures prints nothing.\n- **SC-003**: A threshold equal to the printed percentage never fails the run: `--min-percent 25` on the 25% fixture exits 0.\n- **SC-004**: The existing vitest suite for the script exits 0 with the new cases included.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` and `bc`, both already required by the script | None new - the script already exits 1 when `bc` is absent | Reuse the existing `bc` presence check and integer comparison; add no new tool |\n| Risk | Exit 3 is also the general `spec/*.sh` system-error code | A caller cannot tell \"below threshold\" from \"system error\" by code alone across the script family | Inside this script the system-error paths exit 1 today, so 3 is unambiguous here; record the meaning in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code block |\n| Risk | The comparison drifts from the printed value, e.g. comparing an unrounded `bc` result | The gate and the report disagree | Compare the same rounded integer variable the report prints, and test the boundary where N equals the printed percentage |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns a non-zero comparison into a silent early exit before the report prints | The report disappears on a failing threshold | Make the comparison the last step before the existing `exit`, and assert in a test that the report still prints when the run exits 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. Decisions taken: the option compares the percentage the run reports (`Overall Completion` in folder mode, `Completion` under `--file`); `--json` output is unchanged because only the exit status differs; an invalid value exits 1 rather than 3 so a caller can separate a bad invocation from a failed gate.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
